---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import GridWrapper from "@/components/GridWrapper.astro";
import { siteMetadata } from "@/data/siteMetadata";

// The privacy page Google asks for before a personal tool that signs in with Google may leave
// test mode. It covers those tools only, so it lives under /privacy and leaves /privacy itself
// free for a policy about this website.
const email = siteMetadata.email.replace("mailto:", "");
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy for my personal tools | Kostas Georgiou"
  description="How the small tools I build for myself use Google sign-in."
>
  <div class="relative mt-14">
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <GridWrapper>
        <h1 class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-balance text-center text-4xl font-medium leading-tight tracking-tighter text-text-primary md:text-5xl md:leading-[56px]">
          Privacy for my personal tools
        </h1>
      </GridWrapper>
      <GridWrapper>
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-5 leading-8 text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            Some small tools I build for myself sign in with Google. Only I use them, and they work
            only with my own Google account.
          </p>
          <p>
            Each tool asks Google for the least access it needs. The backup tool asks only for the
            files it creates itself, so it cannot see or change any other file in the account.
          </p>
          <p>
            The sync tool keeps folders on my computer the same as their copies in my Google Drive,
            the way a desktop sync app does. To do that it needs to read and change my Drive files,
            so it asks for that access, and only for my own account.
          </p>
          <p>
            Nothing these tools read is sold, shared with anyone or used for anything else. Backup
            files are encrypted on my computer before they are uploaded. Everything stays in my
            Google Drive until I delete it.
          </p>
          <p>This page is about those tools only, not about this website.</p>
          <p>
            If you have a question about it, please write to me at
            <a class="text-text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href={siteMetadata.email}>{email}</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm">Last updated 15 October 2026.</p>
        </div>
      </GridWrapper>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
